TRIAGE_GRAMMAR = """Triage table grammar (the L1's contract; implement exactly): the table is the first markdown table after a line containing the marker `<!-- sqfs-triage-table v1 -->` inside SKILL.md's `## Queue-drain craft` section (heading line to the next `## ` heading). Header row (exact cell names, in this order): `label | handler | gap kinds | dependencies | -be in child argv | symlink removed | published files | cause -> action | source`. Each data row is one rule; rules are tried top to bottom and the first row whose every condition cell matches gives the label; no match -> `unclassified`. Features taken from an REA extract-firmware envelope (accept both a bare `data` object and a full CLI envelope {ok,data,meta}): H = set of normalized_result.chunks[].handler values that start with `squashfs`; G = set of normalized_result.extraction_gaps[].kind; D = union of extraction_gaps[].dependencies; BE = for every diagnostics[].report whose `command` (string or argv list) names sasquatch: `yes` if any such command has a standalone `-be` token, `no` if such a command exists and none has it, `n/a` if no such command is recorded; SR = `yes` if any normalized_result.diagnostics[].report.__typename__ == `MaliciousSymlinkRemoved` (also accept that typename anywhere under raw_result.report) else `no`; P = len(normalized_result.files). Condition cells (strip surrounding backticks and spaces): `*` matches anything; handler: `none` (H empty) or an fnmatch pattern that must match at least one element of H; gap kinds / dependencies: `none` (empty set) or `a+b` meaning the set equals exactly {a,b} (one name = exactly that singleton); `-be`/symlink removed: `yes`/`no`/`n/a`; published files: `0`, `>0`, or `*`. A malformed cell makes the whole table unevaluable (exit 2), never a silent non-match. The interpreter reads nothing but the table and the envelope."""

